adjust-sharpening-amount
    Amount
adjust-sharpening-radius
    Radius
adjust-sharpening-detail
    Detail
adjust-sharpening-masking
    Masking
adjust-vignette-amount
    Amount
adjust-vignette-midpoint
    Midpoint
adjust-temperature-help
    Higher warms the picture toward yellow; lower cools it toward blue.
adjust-tint-help
    Higher shifts the picture toward magenta; lower shifts it toward green.
adjust-exposure-help
    Higher brightens the whole picture, in stops; bright areas roll off into white rather than clip.
adjust-contrast-help
    Higher darkens the dark tones and brightens the bright ones; lower brings both toward the middle.
adjust-highlights-help
    Lower brings back detail in bright areas; higher brightens them.
adjust-shadows-help
    Higher opens up dark areas; lower deepens them.
adjust-whites-help
    Higher makes the brightest tones brighter; lower pulls them down from white.
adjust-blacks-help
    Lower makes the darkest tones darker; higher lifts them from black.
adjust-clarity-help
    Higher strengthens contrast across broad areas so shapes stand out; lower softens it.
adjust-texture-help
    Higher brings out fine surface detail; lower smooths it, leaving larger edges as they are.
adjust-vibrance-help
    Higher strengthens muted colors more than strong ones; lower mutes them.
adjust-saturation-help
    Higher strengthens every color alike; lower takes color out, to gray at the far left.
adjust-sharpening-amount-help
    Higher sharpens edges more; a stacked result is already sharp, so a little goes a long way.
adjust-sharpening-radius-help
    Higher sharpens a wider band around each edge; lower keeps it to the finest detail.
adjust-sharpening-detail-help
    Higher sharpens the finest detail more; lower holds back halos along large edges.
adjust-sharpening-masking-help
    Higher sharpens only the stronger edges, leaving smooth areas such as a plain background alone.
adjust-vignette-amount-help
    Lower darkens the edges of the picture; higher lightens them.
adjust-vignette-midpoint-help
    Lower starts the vignette nearer the center; higher keeps it to the corners.
adjust-value-stops
    <value> EV
adjust-value-kelvin
    <value> K
adjust-value-pixels
    <value> px
